# Qualcomm Wayland dependencies

The native Qualcomm GBM and EGL drivers still link against the Wayland ABI
and libffi6, even though raylib uses DRM directly and Weston is no longer shipped.
The existing libwayland 1.9.0-1 and libffi6 packages are retained here.
This preserves the current dependencies; it does not establish that the drivers
require this particular Wayland version. PR #502 also reported working with Noble
Wayland libraries: https://github.com/commaai/agnos-builder/pull/502.

Rebuild libwayland-1.9.0-1.deb with build-libwayland-deb.sh.
The libffi6 package comes from Ubuntu Xenial; its armhf counterpart is in libs32.
